abstract: >-
  Open SOC SIEM is a zero-install, browser-based security operations training
  platform. Its Attack Simulator plays six attack scenarios in a simulated SOC,
  including indirect prompt injection against AI agents and federated learning
  poisoning, mapped to MITRE ATT&CK and MITRE ATLAS. Its Log Analyzer lets users
  upload Linux, web server, JSON and CSV logs and returns explained findings with
  a challenge mode and tunable detection rules for teaching. The release also
  includes a threat taxonomy for clinical AI agents, a deterministic synthetic
  labeled dataset, baseline detectors and teaching materials.
